[{"name":"v2.5.0-ce","uuid":"389579213","tag_name":"v2.5.0-ce","target_commitish":"main","body":"## v2.5.0-ce\r\n\r\n### New Features\r\n\r\n* **AI Gateway**\r\n  * Added OpenAI-compatible `/v1/audio/translations` support.\r\n  * Added Anthropic Messages API support through `/v1/messages`.\r\n  * Added hosted CSGHub Responses API support and chat adapter tool handling.\r\n  * Added protocol-wide metrics reporting, dashboard data pipelines, and health checks for chat, responses, embedding, rerank, audio, image, video, OCR, and messages APIs.\r\n  * Added PaddleOCR-VL PaddleX document parsing runtime and improved OCR preprocessing with embedded image support.\r\n\r\n* **Agents \u0026 Sandbox**\r\n  * Added Agent Registry support and the CSGClaw agent type.\r\n  * Added ms-swift agentic job runtime.\r\n  * Integrated CSGClaw instances with Sandbox V2 deploy management.\r\n  * Added configurable CSGClaw sandbox readiness probes and agent names in shared instance responses.\r\n\r\n* **Evaluation \u0026 Finetune**\r\n  * Added staged finetune workflows to reduce runtime cost.\r\n  * Added Claw Eval Codex configuration for OpenAI-compatible API evaluation.\r\n  * Upgraded EvalScope and synchronized dataset rules.\r\n\r\n* **Analytics \u0026 Governance**\r\n  * Added PostHog server-side analytics.\r\n  * Added Redis-backed API rate limiting middleware.\r\n  * Added user API authorization.\r\n  * Added history archive support.\r\n\r\n### Enhancements \u0026 Bug Fixes\r\n\r\n* **AI Gateway Reliability**\r\n  * Migrated protocol handlers to the new pipeline architecture.\r\n  * Fixed billing skips for failed chat, responses, embedding, and rerank requests.\r\n  * Fixed insufficient-balance response handling.\r\n  * Fixed upstream unknown state so it no longer blocks traffic or marks models unavailable.\r\n  * Fixed protocol-specific health-check defaults and Swagger generation ambiguity.\r\n  * Added audio/video/image moderation support.\r\n  * Added generated audio duration capture for TTS responses.\r\n  * Added cached prompt token accounting and usage metering.\r\n\r\n* **Repository, Mirror \u0026 Import**\r\n  * Added organization tag filters.\r\n  * Optimized model index and repository list count queries.\r\n  * Fixed deterministic namespace path lookup.\r\n  * Fixed mirror deletion when the repository was already deleted.\r\n  * Added MCP and Skill repository synchronization.\r\n  * Rejected invalid mirror metadata source URLs.\r\n  * Safely handled large HF NDJSON commit payloads.\r\n  * Optimized skill/code package import and S3 package sync.\r\n\r\n* **Deploy, Resource \u0026 Runtime**\r\n  * Checked cluster status for serverless detail queries and added force-stop support.\r\n  * Improved deploy updates when clusters are offline.\r\n  * Added serverless status filtering and multi-status query support.\r\n  * Added XPU memory size support for physical XPU and MIG resources.\r\n  * Added APIs to update space resource scenario constraints.\r\n  * Added Ascend NPU runtime images and Ascend 910 HAMI support.\r\n  * Added TGI ROCm inference image and updated llama-factory AMD engine support.\r\n\r\n* **Security \u0026 Access Control**\r\n  * Fixed API key leakage in logs.\r\n  * Protected `/events` from unauthorized clients exhausting database resources.\r\n  * Added private endpoint permission checks for inference and version access.\r\n  * Added feature-gating groundwork with OpenFeature and license integration.\r\n  * Added sensitive-check gating for agent templates.\r\n\r\n* **Accounting \u0026 Reporting**\r\n  * Added token usage information to evaluation summaries.\r\n  * Added LLM log curated dataflow email notifications.\r\n  * Reported source line and dataset row counts in LLM log sync emails.\r\n  * Applied global timezone handling to admin queries, export data, recharge ranges, and accounting bills.\r\n  * Capped accounting export page size to the upstream per-page limit.\r\n  * Used `recorded_at` for AccountStatements and AccountMeterings partitioning.\r\n\r\n### Maintenance\r\n\r\n* Updated ms-swift configuration and Dockerfiles.\r\n* Upgraded agent-sandbox to v0.5.4.\r\n* Bumped GitPython to 3.1.58 and 3.1.61 in relevant runtime requirements.\r\n* Updated GitHub Actions checkout and setup-go workflow versions, pinning Go 1.26.\r\n* Fixed lint and stabilized database/user-like tests.\r\n* Regenerated mocks for exported availability interfaces only.\r\n* Added agent and merge request contract documentation.\r\n\r\n### New Contributors\r\n\r\n* @sabhi128 made their first contribution in https://github.com/OpenCSGs/csghub-server/pull/1304\r\n* @katsugtgz made their first contribution in https://github.com/OpenCSGs/csghub-server/pull/1349\r\n* @vaibhav8a made their first contribution in https://github.com/OpenCSGs/csghub-server/pull/1411\r\n* @xrwang8 made their first contribution in https://github.com/OpenCSGs/csghub-server/pull/1414","draft":false,"prerelease":false,"immutable":false,"published_at":"2026-09-16T01:30:06.000Z","created_at":"2026-09-19T05:21:30.876Z","author":"Rader","assets":[],"last_synced_at":"2026-09-19T05:21:30.152Z","html_url":"https://github.com/OpenCSGs/csghub/releases/tag/v2.5.0-ce","release_url":"https://repos.ecosyste.ms/api/v1/hosts/GitHub/repositories/OpenCSGs%2Fcsghub/releases/v2.5.0-ce","tag_url":"https://repos.ecosyste.ms/api/v1/hosts/GitHub/repositories/OpenCSGs%2Fcsghub/tags/v2.5.0-ce"}]